From: Atharva Tiwari <atharvatiwarilinuxdev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/pm: Fix boot problems in 5300

This fixes the error:
"SMU: I'm not done with your previous command" on 5300.

This is not upstreamable.
We currently don't know how macOS derives these values,
so we only know the hardcoded values provided by ioreg.

Only the AMD Radeon Pro 5300M of the MacBookPro16,1 (PCI 1002:7340,
subsystem 106b:0219) takes the new path; every other GPU is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Atharva Tiwari <atharvatiwarilinuxdev@gmail.com>

Source (pinned): t2linux linux-t2-patches
commit b3fac289b2e46797c6e403078df1567214920324, file
6001-drm-amd-pm-Fix-boot-problems-in-5300.patch
(https://github.com/t2linux/linux-t2-patches). Rebased by IYAKKI onto
6.12.112: the same code, inserted before 6.12's bitmap_empty() check (later
kernels renamed it smu_feature_list_is_empty()). Licence: GPL-2.0 (kernel
code). Carried for the optional Mac image variant only.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu11/smu_v11_0.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu11/smu_v11_0.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu11/smu_v11_0.c
index 7fda51724..1d70d0a96 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu11/smu_v11_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu11/smu_v11_0.c
@@ -746,6 +746,22 @@ int smu_v11_0_set_allowed_mask(struct smu_context *smu)
 	int ret = 0;
 	uint32_t feature_mask[2];
 
+	if (smu->adev->pdev->vendor == 0x1002 && smu->adev->pdev->device == 0x7340 &&
+			smu->adev->pdev->subsystem_vendor == 0x106B &&
+			smu->adev->pdev->subsystem_device == 0x0219) {
+		ret = smu_cmn_send_smc_msg_with_param(smu, SMU_MSG_SetAllowedFeaturesMaskLow,
+				0xABC9AFBB, NULL);
+		if (ret)
+			goto failed;
+
+		ret = smu_cmn_send_smc_msg_with_param(smu, SMU_MSG_SetAllowedFeaturesMaskHigh,
+				0xFFFFFD42, NULL);
+		if (ret)
+			goto failed;
+
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	if (bitmap_empty(feature->allowed, SMU_FEATURE_MAX) || feature->feature_num < 64) {
 		ret = -EINVAL;
 		goto failed;
